"""Document highlight detail coverage and the reference/approximation boundary."""
from pathlib import Path
import json
r=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1];pkg=json.loads((r/'package.json').read_text())['name'];records=[x for x in json.loads((r/'output/buildings.json').read_text())if x['landmark']]
title={'umich-ann-arbor-model':'UMich','ucsb-campus-model':'UC Santa Barbara','uchicago-hydepark-model':'UChicago'}[pkg]
text=f'''# {title} highlight refinement\n\nAll {len(records)} architectural highlights are individually reviewed in [the architectural form audit](HIGHLIGHT_ARCHITECTURE_AUDIT.md). That audit records source-specific reconstructions and the individual forms retained after review. The component table below documents joinery only; a frame count is not architectural verification. This remains a public-source exterior interpretation; opening positions and member dimensions are not a measured facade survey.\n\nShaped reveals follow the existing glass outlines, including pointed Gothic heads. Frames and transoms remain within each opening zone. Coping follows actual roof triangles, including concave plans, and stays supported on its roof finish. No automatic rooftop equipment boxes or arbitrary full-height facade rods are introduced. Repeated components retain separate material/feature ownership.\n\n'''
if pkg=='umich-ann-arbor-model':
 text+='''Kahn Pavilion receives deeper light precast reveals, informed by the architect's photographed three-dimensional facade panels. Burton and Lurie carillons have hollow flared bell shells rather than solid cone placeholders. Bell arrangements and sizes are approximate. The current Burton facility page states 53 bells, while some other university descriptions state 55; this model does not claim an instrument survey.\n\n- [Kahn Pavilion — HOK](https://www.hok.com/projects/view/michigan-medicine-kahn-health-care-pavilion/)\n- [Baird Carillon — SMTD](https://smtd.umich.edu/facilities/burton-memorial-tower/charles-baird-carillon/)\n- [Lurie Carillon — SMTD](https://smtd.umich.edu/facilities/ann-and-robert-h-lurie-carillon/)\n\nThe existing overview and near-detail regional delivery is regenerated from the final architecture, retaining its bounded detail budgets.\n\n'''
elif pkg=='ucsb-campus-model':
 text+='''Campbell Hall separates the lecture-hall drum from lower wings and uses an alternating folded-plate roof plus tall plaza glazing, interpreted from the owner's exterior photograph. Kohn Hall separates its warm gate-facing tower and low wings; the courtyard concavity is retained from the map and receives a supported, partly open high awning and paving, using the public two-floor plan as a layout reference. Bioengineering uses three storeys in accordance with the department facilities description. Storke contains 61 hollow bell forms; their mounts and sizes are approximate. Harder Stadium adds guardrails supported on its upper modeled grandstand tread.\n\n- [Campbell Hall plaza photograph — AAIT](https://aait.ucsb.edu/event-av-services/campbell-hall/gallery)\n- [Kohn Hall architecture — KITP](https://www.kitp.ucsb.edu/news/new-kohn-hall)\n- [Kohn Hall public plan — KITP](https://www.kitp.ucsb.edu/sites/default/files/kitp/maps/KITPemergencymap.png)\n- [Bioengineering facilities — department](https://bioengineering.ucsb.edu/facilities)\n- [Storke Tower — university](https://www.campuscalendar.ucsb.edu/storke_tower)\n\nThe campus keeps its existing full campus renderer. Regional LOD continues to apply only to Isla Vista and neighboring areas.\n\n'''
else:
 text+='''Hutchinson Commons is rebuilt as a single great-hall storey with tall pointed openings, exterior buttresses and a steep slate roof, replacing generic repeated classroom floors. Larger Gothic openings are retained within their modeled storey zones. Modern highlights receive close-range framed glazing and roof coping while keeping their existing distinctive massing.\n\n- [Tower Group — university architecture reference](https://architecture.uchicago.edu/locations/tower_group_mitchell_tower_hutchinson_commons_reynolds_club_mandel_hall/)\n\n'''
text+='| Code | Highlight | Framed openings | Transoms | Roof coping (m) | Reference |\n|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---|\n'
for b in records:
 s=b['highlight_joinery'];ref=b.get('highlight_reference')or b.get('architecture_reference')or b.get('source');
 if isinstance(ref,dict):ref=next(iter(ref.get('sources',[{}])),{}).get('url','https://architecture.uchicago.edu/')
 text+=f"| {b['code']} | {b['name'].replace('|','/')} | {s['framed_openings']} | {s['transoms']} | {s['roof_coping_m']:.2f} | [Reference]({ref}) |\n"
text+='\nCoverage and exported bell counts are checked by `scripts/check_highlights.py`. CAD import, compressed-byte integrity, existing navigation checks and concise representative near-view browser checks are used for validation.\n'
(r/'docs/HIGHLIGHT_REFINEMENT.md').write_text(text)
